{"study_accession":"PRJNA1149481","secondary_study_accession":"SRP527210","title":"Antiretroviral Therapy at Conception Leads to Lower Peripheral CD49a+ NK Cells and Higher SERPINB2.","description":"Antiretroviral therapy (ART) during pregnancy is essential to prevent vertical HIV transmission and preserve the health of the mother and child. However, ART in pregnancy has been associated with adverse birth outcomes linked to poor placental development. Immune dysregulation of placental development is an important factor in the development of pre-eclampsia (PE), a common hypertension disorder of pregnancy. Some studies found an association between ART use at conception or during the first trimester and PE. To investigate the immune environment in pregnant persons with HIV (PPWH) on ART at conception (N=40) compared to PPWH that started ART in the 2nd trimester (N=40) we analyzed data from the International Maternal Pediatric Adolescent AIDS Clinical Trials (IMPAACT) Perinatal Core Protocol, P1025, concluded in 2013. No difference was found in soluble factors in circulation including PlGF and sFLt-1, associated with PE. However, upon analysis of PBMC by high dimension flow cytometry, we detected a lower frequency of circulating CD49a+ NK cells, associated with uterine tissue and pregnancy, in PPWH on ART at conception compared with PPWH who started ART in the 2nd trimester. Moreover, PBMC from PPWH on ART at conception expressed higher levels of SERPINB2 in transcriptomics analyses. Our findings shed new insights into the potential impact of ART at conception and suggest the persistence of a dysregulated inflammatory environment compared to PPWH starting ART after the conclusion of placental development. Overall design: Total RNA of PBMC was extracted from a subset of 20 PPWH per group (chosen based on sample availability and to maintain matched characteristics) using the RNAeasy Kit (Qiagen) following manufacturer recommendations. Due to the low RNA yield, a low-input RNA-seq library preparation was performed, and samples were sequenced at the NUSeq Core using 3 lanes of the Illumina HiSeq 4000 (50bp, single-read) yielding >22M reads per sample. Data were analyzed using the Partek Flow software. 40 Pregnant Persons with HIV (PPWH), PBMC, 2 Treatment Groups (On cART at conception vs Initiated cART at ≥2nd trimester)","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":40,"study_labels":[],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN43245160","study_accession":"PRJNA1149481","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"EM-40_2nd tr","description":"EM-40_2nd tr","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM8465913","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2025-06-03","attributes":[["source_name","PBMC"],["cell_type","PBMC"],["group of_women","Initiated cART at ≥ 2nd trimester"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR30290996","experiment_accession":"SRX25751713","library_layout":"SINGLE","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 4000","read_count":30096060,"base_count":1504803000,"first_public":"2025-06-03","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 4000 sequencing: GSM8465913: EM-40_2nd tr Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN43245161","study_accession":"PRJNA1149481","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"EM-39_2nd tr","description":"EM-39_2nd tr","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM8465912","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2025-06-23","attributes":[["source_name","PBMC"],["cell_type","PBMC"],["group of_women","Initiated cART at ≥ 2nd trimester"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR30290997","experiment_accession":"SRX25751712","library_layout":"SINGLE","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 4000","read_count":35466031,"base_count":1773301550,"first_public":"2025-06-23","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 4000 sequencing: GSM8465912: EM-39_2nd tr Hom